				==============================
				PREDICT-NG QUICK START GUIDE
				==============================

SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS
===================
- C compiler (gcc or clang)
- ncurses library (libncurses-dev or equivalent)
- pthreads (included in libc on Linux)
- math library (libm)
- wget (for kepupdate)

Optional:
- /dev/dsp soundcard for voice announcements (vocalizer)


COMPILATION AND INSTALLATION
=============================
	./configure
	make
	sudo make install

The default install prefix is /usr/local. To change it:

	./configure --prefix=/usr

To build the optional vocalizer (requires /dev/dsp):

	./configure --enable-vocalizer

For a full list of options:

	./configure --help


FIRST TIME USE
==============
On first run, predict-ng will prompt for your ground station location:

  - Latitude in decimal degrees North (negative for South)
  - Longitude in decimal degrees East (negative for West)
  - Altitude in meters above sea level

Run kepupdate to fetch current Keplerian orbital data from Celestrak:

	kepupdate

To automate daily TLE updates, add to your crontab (crontab -e):

	0 2 * * * kepupdate


FOR FURTHER INFORMATION
=======================
See the man page:

	man predict

or the files under the docs/ subdirectory.


Happy Tracking!

